{"id":"9ae304110b216a5dd145f619d9e47bda3b919ceb669df36e4fc37c57f2025a81","at":"2026-10-13T19:47:07Z","commit":"453d75cbece2ee702d49853d849c53334c8acf8c","parents":["24648505ab3792fa97ae2551578733527b60ff94f26bf1981a5ce3bbf8275bb2"],"op":"relate","type":"implements","ends":[{"kind":"code","id":"ExTLA.ModelChecker.Parallel","hash":"89bf07d4"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/04-layer2-model-checker.md#Layer 2: Specification DSL + Model Checker/Per-declaration cost — `ExTLA.Profile`/Under `--workers`","hash":"e451e4e8"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"#413 review at surfex 0.8.0, whose version of Parallel now covers its hidden code (expand_batch/2, zeroed/1, merge/2, merge_outcome/2, merge_profile/2, batches/2, concurrency/1), all read. Section claims checked against it: each batch starts from a zeroed graph, a fresh Coverage.init and Profile.zero, and reads Profile.collect plus its own reduction bracket before the task ends; merge/2 sums contributions via Coverage.merge/2 and Profile.merge. The test reaches Parallel through run/2 and checks the coordinator's contribution is merged in: type_ok's evaluations are nonzero at 1 and 8 workers, which fails if only workers' accumulators were merged. The section's later 'run_reductions remains the coordinator's figure' paragraph contradicts finalize/2 and is filed separately.","basis":"review"}
