{"id":"cb838a439cff8918b71acb3a4ddb494197ce5a2e0f34dd4f92bb3c204259c338","at":"2026-10-13T20:35:14Z","commit":"eefa715b784e55b105b3250f68f9a93ee517ec08","parents":["6f8c7379813f307734fb9b10112e0cbc3ed359c40c36dcedd8e262d45a279efe"],"op":"relate","type":"implements","ends":[{"kind":"code","id":"Mix.Tasks.Extla.Check","hash":"584301af"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/04-layer2-model-checker.md#Layer 2: Specification DSL + Model Checker/Mix Integration/Mix Task: `mix extla.check`/The JSON result schema","hash":"69b27103"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"#387 review. Rule 3 (absent is null, never 0) rests on Coverage reporting an unmeasured near-miss count as nil (coverage.ex:119, kept nil through merge at :352); the task copies Coverage's report into the coverage block. The test runs NoBranch, whose invariant has no top-level or and so nothing to measure, and asserts its near_misses is exactly null: a default to 0 fails it.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"eb353caf82a6044891744c08ba3501ac728afd336ad12dcf0ffa8edd4ec3ece1","at":"2026-10-13T20:35:18Z","commit":"eefa715b784e55b105b3250f68f9a93ee517ec08","parents":["97c93aa31a506c43a3feb93bb74a2438ba6e3fb59d9481415f763c9373ecc7a2"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Mix.Tasks.Extla.CheckTest: the JSON result schema's coverage and profile blocks: reductions is the floor times the evaluations, with observed kept beside it","hash":"66606c6e"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/04-layer2-model-checker.md#Layer 2: Specification DSL + Model Checker/Mix Integration/Mix Task: `mix extla.check`/The JSON result schema","hash":"69b27103"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"#387 review. The section: reductions is per_eval * evaluations with per_eval the floor, observed kept beside it. Profile.finalize/2 computes reductions from the floor and keeps observed; the task writes each declaration. The test asserts the identity and an integer observed for every declaration; writing observed as reductions fails it.","basis":"review"}
