{"id":"1dcb31a16d9768a4300ce2b6b96e953a90a32843528aad1c6130c6b1e169ffe0","at":"2026-10-13T20:35:22Z","commit":"eefa715b784e55b105b3250f68f9a93ee517ec08","parents":["b3ead2c24440345bc7e2553dee5fb51470198fed4aa74447d7c1e60e1b4575f1"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Mix.Tasks.Extla.CheckTest: the JSON result schema's coverage and profile blocks: a profile carries its documented keys, and each declaration describes itself","hash":"841c2ce2"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/04-layer2-model-checker.md#Layer 2: Specification DSL + Model Checker/Mix Integration/Mix Task: `mix extla.check`/The JSON result schema","hash":"69b27103"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"#387 review. The section's profile block carries run_reductions, otp_version, calibration and declarations, a sorted list of self-describing entries (kind, name, evaluations, reductions, per_eval, observed). The test asserts both key sets exactly and the sort; an unsorted encoder fails it.","basis":"review"}
